From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:37:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: Let a property take the VARIANT type its CIM type
 is read back as.

WMI gives a uint32 as VT_I4, and a method parameter of that type takes
VT_I4 too; putting it failed with WBEM_E_TYPE_MISMATCH.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/wbemprox/class.c b/dlls/wbemprox/class.c
index b1e5794567b..0986ae52d5c 100644
--- a/dlls/wbemprox/class.c
+++ b/dlls/wbemprox/class.c
@@ -417,7 +417,10 @@ static HRESULT record_set_value( struct record *record, UINT index, VARIANT *var
     HRESULT hr;
 
     if ((hr = to_longlong( var, &val, &type )) != S_OK) return hr;
-    if (type != record->fields[index].type) return WBEM_E_TYPE_MISMATCH;
+    /* a property also takes the VARIANT type its CIM type is read back as, VT_I4 for a uint32 */
+    if (type != record->fields[index].type && V_VT( var ) != to_vartype( record->fields[index].type ))
+        return WBEM_E_TYPE_MISMATCH;
+    type = record->fields[index].type;
 
     if (type & CIM_FLAG_ARRAY)
     {
